WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.846
TRACE is search that shows its work.

2
00:00:03.196 --> 00:00:04.617
You ask in plain words.

3
00:00:04.617 --> 00:00:07.570
It finds the passages that match your meaning,

4
00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:10.009
and gives you a record you can check.

5
00:00:10.809 --> 00:00:13.645
Ask an AI to search a huge pile of text,

6
00:00:13.645 --> 00:00:15.276
and you get an answer.

7
00:00:15.626 --> 00:00:17.156
But where did it come from?

8
00:00:17.156 --> 00:00:19.082
What did it miss? You can't tell.

9
00:00:19.882 --> 00:00:23.466
So here is the real thing, running in a browser.

10
00:00:23.466 --> 00:00:27.848
The library behind it holds about 800 thousand passages.

11
00:00:28.898 --> 00:00:30.155
Pick a question.

12
00:00:32.105 --> 00:00:36.192
Results come up: passages that match what the question means,

13
00:00:36.192 --> 00:00:37.532
not just its words.

14
00:00:38.782 --> 00:00:39.787
Click one.

15
00:00:41.537 --> 00:00:43.327
Here is its checkable record:

16
00:00:43.327 --> 00:00:46.340
the article it came from, where in the article,

17
00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:48.713
and a fingerprint of the exact text.

18
00:00:49.863 --> 00:00:52.213
Press check, and your own browser works

19
00:00:52.213 --> 00:00:54.564
out the fingerprint again. It matches.

20
00:00:58.114 --> 00:00:59.535
Now the key question.

21
00:00:59.535 --> 00:01:02.635
Is this the same answer as the exact method,

22
00:01:02.635 --> 00:01:04.607
which checks every passage?

23
00:01:05.557 --> 00:01:09.171
Here, the ten passages are the same, in the same order.

24
00:01:11.521 --> 00:01:13.138
On our test searches,

25
00:01:13.138 --> 00:01:16.837
TRACE looked at under 1 percent of the library,

26
00:01:16.837 --> 00:01:20.766
and still found 99.85 percent of the exact answer.

27
00:01:21.716 --> 00:01:25.735
Far less scoring work, and every result shows where it came from.

28
00:01:28.085 --> 00:01:30.506
Try another question. Same idea:

29
00:01:30.506 --> 00:01:34.642
ranked passages, a record, and a side-by-side check.

30
00:01:38.192 --> 00:01:40.824
An answer you can check, not just trust.

31
00:01:41.624 --> 00:01:44.532
To use it, open the page in your web browser.

32
00:01:44.532 --> 00:01:48.351
There is nothing to install, and nothing to sign up for.

33
00:01:48.701 --> 00:01:49.913
It is a small page,

34
00:01:49.913 --> 00:01:52.783
and any computer with a web browser will do.

35
00:01:53.133 --> 00:01:56.119
A kit to run it on your own computer is planned,

36
00:01:56.119 --> 00:01:57.302
but not built yet.

37
00:01:58.102 --> 00:01:59.632
Now, the honest limits.

38
00:01:59.632 --> 00:02:02.892
Ordinary keyword search did better on our test,

39
00:02:02.892 --> 00:02:04.488
and it answers faster.

40
00:02:04.838 --> 00:02:06.577
Exact meaning-based search,

41
00:02:06.577 --> 00:02:09.412
with no shortcut, did no better than TRACE.

42
00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:13.203
TRACE is for search by meaning that you can verify.

43
00:02:13.553 --> 00:02:15.596
The public live server is off,

44
00:02:15.596 --> 00:02:19.001
so this explorer replays real recorded questions.

45
00:02:19.351 --> 00:02:22.785
It has not been run on public benchmark tests yet,

46
00:02:22.785 --> 00:02:25.396
and no outside group has verified it.

47
00:02:26.196 --> 00:02:29.285
Try it: open the explorer, link on screen.

48
00:02:29.635 --> 00:02:32.863
Next up: a kit to run it on your own computer.

